    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "5. Kinship terms\n\nAnother instance of the in-group/out-group distinction shows up in the use of kinship terms. (In this case, in-group members are one's own family members and out-group members are another person's family members.)\n\n(my)            (other's)\nshujin          goshujin        husband\nkanai           okusan          wife\n\nThe following is a summary of the use of kore and kochira with kinship terms.\n\nkore + in-group kinship terms\n\nkochira + out-group kinship terms"
    }
